leave_policies = """1.1. Purpose of the Leave Policy
To provide employees with time away from their job for rest, relaxation and personal pursuits. To facilitate a culture of work-life balance.
1.2. Annual Leave Entitlement
All full time regular employees are entitled to leaves up to a pre-determined limit, as detailed below:
Criteria Total Entitlement
Confirmed Employees 16 days per annum
Trainees/Consultants 1 day per month
1.3. Leave Break-up
Casual/Sick Leave - 7 Days
Casual/Sick Leave days are use or lose days, un-availed leaves would get lapsed at the end of the year i.e., no carry forward or encashment nor any eligibility for payout upon separation from employment.
Earned Leave - 9 Days
Earned Leave is the paid leave i.e. must either be availed or en-cashed at the end of the calendar year. Ideally, annual leave entitlements should be exhausted annually as Company encourages time offs instead of payouts.
Company Holidays - 10 Days
Besides Sick, Casual & Earned leave every year our company observes ten days as official company holidays on account of National holidays/festivals. The specific dates for each year are declared annually, at the beginning of each year in accordance with the Government of India Holidays.
Compensatory Leave
In case employees are required to work on a holiday, they are eligible for compensatory leave. An employee will be eligible for a compensatory leave only if he/she has worked 8 hours on the holiday. Compensatory leave will be provided at the discretion of the respective Team Lead. Employee is required to send request for the same on ERP and need to take approval from Lead/PM within a week of the day worked on. It is compulsory to use some tracker (Hub staff/Upwork/or any other as decided by company from time to time) and provide the details via ERP.
1.4. Leave Calculation Process
All leave entitlements are determined for the calendar year i.e. from 1st Jan. to 31st Dec.
Leave days are credited at the beginning of the calendar year but are not earned until accrued in accordance with policy.
Members joining or leaving anytime in-between the year would get their leave calculated on pro-rata basis. Members who terminate their employment with the Company and have used leave in excess of their entitlement will be required to repay the Company amounts in excess (if any).
Members joining or leaving anytime in-between the year would get their leave calculated on pro-rata basis. Members who terminate their employment with the Company and have used leave in excess of their entitlement will be required to repay the Company amounts in excess (if any).
Sandwich Policy:
Any leaves applied on working days and combined with a holiday and a weekend results in treating the weekend as leaves.
For eg: For the year 2020 as per holidays list two examples are given below 24th Dec 2019 and 2nd Jan 2020 will be counted as 4 leaves 10th Jan 2020 and 14th Jan 2020 will be counted as 4 leaves
Any leaves applied on working days and combined with a weekend in between results in treating the weekend as leaves. Leave on both Friday and subsequent Monday will be counted as 4 leaves
5+2 Rule: In case leave is taken for entire workweek then weekend at end of leaves will also be counted as leaves.
One weekend in a year per employee will be waived off from the sandwich policy. The waiver is available for the confirmed employees only.
1.5. Leave taken during Probation Period
If a member leaves the company before completing six months of service, then earned leaves availed during his/her stay in the company will be deducted from his/her final settlement. In addition, leave is neither en-cashable nor adjustable against the notice period if an employee resigns before completing six months of service. Six months of service means employee’s presence in office for 180 days ie leaves will not be considered.
1.6. For Members on Training
Leave entitlement is one leave per month during training period.
Leave cannot be carried forward.
Leave cannot be en-cashed.
Any extra leaves taken will result in the date of confirmation as employee being extended by same
1.7. Leave Application Process
Approval for leave is taken through ERP ONLY.
The Immediate Supervisor/Manager recommends leave.
Leave equal to or more than four days requires the Director’s/ Founder’s approval or PM/TL who are directly reporting to Upper Management.
For all leaves, employees should send request via ERP and can proceed with leaves after approval.
Under exceptional circumstances (i.e., sickness or urgent work) if the member is not able to apply for leave beforehand he/she must inform their respective Managers/Supervisor as soon as possible and should apply via ERP on the day he/she returns from leave.
If absent without Leave sanction/ approval or beyond eligibility, the absence would be considered as Leave without Pay (LWP).
Employees are required to adhere to office timings i.e. entry between 9:00 am to 10:00 am and complete 9 office hours and 8 work hours every day. In absence of non-completion of work hours & office hours leaves will be deducted as applicable.
It is the responsibility of each member to maintain his/her individual account of leave and plan leaves keeping in view the work requirements.
1.8. Maternity Leave
Confirmed female employees will be eligible for Maternity Leave as per Maternity Benefit Act 1961 and Maternity-Benefit-Act- NOTIFICATION-29.03.2017
Note: This benefit is not available to employees on probation
1.9. Leave Encashment Policy
Applicable only in case of the balance Earned leaves (if any) at the end of the calendar year.
Unutilized Earned Leaves balance (if any) would be en-cashed at end of the calendar year i.e., in the month of December or at the time of separation.
Leave Encashment will be calculated on the basic salary drawn. In case of increment during the calendar year, leave encashment will be calculated on pro-rata basis."""